Wyndham has introduced a $95 annual paid loyalty program, Wyndham Rewards I=
nsider, which provides=20
members with hotel discounts, automatic gold status, bonus points, and savi=
ngs on flights and=20
cruises. This marks a significant experiment in subscription-based loyalty =
by a U.S. hotel group.=20
While the program seeks to drive greater customer engagement and compete wi=
th credit card rewards,=20
it must overcome challenges related to infrequent travel habits, partner co=
ordination, and=20
demonstrating consistent value to subscribers.

